        {
            "Section": "IT.DDYN",
            "Unnamed: 1": "DDYN",
            "Unnamed: 2": "Were any death detail assessments collected? [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "text",
            "Unnamed: 4": 1,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": "CL.C66742.NY.NY",
            "Unnamed: 7": 3,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "DDYN [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "DDYN [CDASH]\nIndicate if the death details are known. If yes, include the appropriate details where indicated on the CRF. [completionInstructions]\nThe intent/purpose of collecting this field is to help with data cleaning and monitoring. It provides verification if all other fields on the CRF were deliberately left blank. [implementationNotes]\nDoes not map to an SDTMIG variable. The SDTM Annotated CRF is annotated to indicate that this field is NOT SUBMITTED. [mappingInstructions]\nAny Death Detail Assessments [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 15": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 16": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 17": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 18": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 19": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 20": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 21": NaN
        },
        {
            "Section": "IT.[DTHDXCD]_DDDAT",
            "Unnamed: 1": "DDDAT",
            "Unnamed: 2": "What was the date [DTHDX] assessment was collected?\nCollection Date [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "date",
            "Unnamed: 4": 2,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 7": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "DDDAT [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "DDDAT [CDASH]\nRecord the date of collection using this format (DD-MON-YYYY). [completionInstructions]\nA single date may be collected for all death detail assessments when they are collected on the same date. The date of collection of each assessment can also be collected using a CDASH variable [DTHDXCD]_DDDAT. The date of the assessment may be determined from a collected date of visit and in such cases a separate assessment date field is not required. [implementationNotes]\nThis does not map directly to an SDTMIG variable. For the SDTM submission dataset, concatenate all collected CDASH DATE and TIME components and populate the SDTMIG variable DDDTC in ISO 8601 format. [mappingInstructions]\n[DTHDX] Date [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 15": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 16": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 17": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 18": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 19": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 20": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 21": NaN
        },
        {
            "Section": "IT.DTHDAT",
            "Unnamed: 1": "DTHDAT",
            "Unnamed: 2": "What [is/was] the subject's date of death?\nDeath Date [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "date",
            "Unnamed: 4": 3,
            "Unnamed: 5": "No",
            "Unnamed: 6": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 7": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "DTHDAT [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "DTHDAT [CDASH]\nRecord the date of death. [completionInstructions]\nThe CDASH model defines Death Date as a timing variable; this is not included as a timing variable in the SDTMIG. It may be collected on any CRF deemed appropriate by the sponsor, but should only be collected once. The SDTMIG variable DTHDTC is mapped to the DM domain during the SDTM submission dataset creation process. The SDTMIG variable DM.DTHFLG is not a CDASH variable, but it is typically populated during the SDTM submission dataset creation process. Death Date may be mapped to other SDTM domains, as deemed appropriate by the sponsor (e.g., DS). [implementationNotes]\nThis field does not map directly to an SDTMIG variable. For the SDTM dataset, concatenate all collected CDASH DATE and TIME components and populate the SDTM variable DTHDTC in ISO 8601 format. [mappingInstructions]\nDeath Date [prompt]",
            "Unnamed: 12": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 13": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 14": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 15": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 16": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 17": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 18": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 19": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 20": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 21": NaN
        },
        {
            "Section": "IT.[DTHDXCD]_DDORRES",
            "Unnamed: 1": "PRCDTH_DDORRES",
            "Unnamed: 2": "What was the primary cause of death? [en]",
            "Unnamed: 3": "text",
            "Unnamed: 4": 4,
            "Unnamed: 5": "Yes",
            "Unnamed: 6": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 7": 15,
            "Unnamed: 8": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 9": NaN,
            "Unnamed: 10": "PRCDTH_DDORRES [en]",
            "Unnamed: 11": "PRCDTH_DDORRES [CDASH]\nRecord the death detail response. [completionInstructions]\nEach test may be collected using the CDASH variable [TESTCD] (e.g., PRCDTH) or [TESTCD]_DDORRES where TESTCD is the appropriate CT for the DD test code e.g., PRCDTH_DDORRES. This CDASH variable name is an example of what \"variable name\" can be used in a denormalized data structure. [implementationNotes]\nMaps directly to the SDTMIG variable listed in the column with the heading SDTMIG Target. In addition to the SDTMIG variable DDORRES, create DDTESTCD from the CDASH variable name and determine the value of DDTEST from DDTESTCD. The CDASH prompt may also contain the DDTEST. Use appropriate CDISC Controlled Terminology for the test and test code. [mappingInstructions]\nResult [prompt]",
